Rule 1 (number of partitions must be at least 1)
{v_3 : int} |= v_3 ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (partitions shape must be a prefix of data shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) ∧ (if ndim(v_2) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 3 (partition indices are non-negative when scalar or non-empty)
{v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = 0 then min(v_2) ≥ 0 else if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0 then true else min(v_2) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (partition indices are less than the number of partitions when scalar or non-empty)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if ndim(v_2) = 0 then max(v_2) ≤ v_3 - 1 else if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0 then true else max(v_2) ≤ v_3 - 1
>>
Rule 5 (exactly one partition implies all indices are 0 unless partitions is empty)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_3 = 1 then (if ndim(v_2) = 0 then min(v_2) = 0 ∧ max(v_2) = 0 else if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0 then true else min(v_2) = 0 ∧ max(v_2) = 0)
>>
Rule 6 (vector partitions must match data’s leading dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = 1 then ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 7 (zero-sized partition dimensions imply corresponding zero-sized data dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : (shape(v_2, i) ≠ 0 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 0)
